--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 6dffa7a9e72b4c04c9a385c19a34608a, type: 3}
  m_Name: Module4_TrainingDefinition
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::BitsPilani.Module4.Module4Definition
  homeScene: Module4_Home
  walkScene: Module4_Walk
  initialLoadSeconds: 6
  homeObservationSeconds: 20
  walkObservationSeconds: 20
  flashbackSeconds: 20
  responseObservationSeconds: 10
  replayObservationSeconds: 20
  responseDialoguePauseSeconds: 2.5
  fadeSeconds: 0.2
  guidedPractice: 1
  requireParticipantId: 1
  requireSavedAnswer: 1
  childEyeView: 1
  childEyeHeight: 1.05
  clues:
  - He stopped walking
  - He is crying without using words
  - He keeps looking towards the park
  - His body looks tense
  - The park entrance is beside the path
  - The mall is in the other direction
  - No destination was explained at home
  - He got ready in his usual going-out routine
  - His shoes seem uncomfortable
  - He seems tired after a long walk
  - He may have noticed something unfamiliar
  - He is asking for a snack
  guesses:
  - He expected to visit the park
  - He is scared of something nearby
  - He wants to stop walking
  - He does not like this place
  - He does not know where we are going
  - He finds an unexpected change difficult
  - He is uncomfortable or tired
  - He needs help understanding today's plan
  confidence:
  - Not sure
  - Somewhat sure
  - Very sure
  responses:
  - Show pictures of today's plan
  - 'Calmly explain: Today we are going to the mall, then home.'
  - Reassure him we can talk once we reach the mall
  - Repeat the instruction more firmly to make it clear
  prevention:
  - Use a picture plan before leaving
  - Explain today's destination before leaving
  - Keep the familiar routine so he feels reassured
  - Explain the destination if he asks on the way
  questions:
  - What did you first think was happening?
  - What changed your mind?
  - What did your child need?
  feedback: Your child may have expected a park trip because getting ready looked
    the same as before. You knew you were going to the mall, but he had not been
    told. His reaction can be a sign that what happened did not match what he expected.
    A simple explanation or picture plan before leaving can help him understand what
    comes next.
